From 3ed3dce555b7a790903170b799c8a8bd4237245c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 11:02:11 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 187/191] Native movies with subtitles

- ga2_movie: the games' movies (PSS: MPEG-2 640x480, 16-bit 48 kHz stereo PCM in private stream 1) played by the
  PC. A thread reads the movie's sectors (the disc image, or the mod overlay past its end), demuxes the program
  stream itself (video to FFmpeg's mpeg2video parser and decoder, the SShd/SSbd audio de-interleaved), converts
  pictures with swscale; the audio is mixed into the SPU2 output stream (ps2_audio's callback) and is the clock;
  pictures are shown by frame number against it. FFmpeg calls available from 4.x to 8 only (the release's static
  FFmpeg already has the parts used).
- Subtitles: <pack>/subtitles/<program>/<file>.srt (or GA2_SUBTITLE_DIR), drawn with the UI font under the
  picture, into a render texture with the picture so the headset's screen shows them too.
- Presented in place of the game's picture (desktop and VR theater screen), as a 4:3 bilinear picture.
- Settings "Movies" (movies: native / original, GA2_MOVIES) and "Movie subtitles" (movie_subtitles, GA2_MOVIE_
  SUBTITLES). The game hooks are in native/compat/ga2_movie.cpp.
- ps2_runtime: also includes the game thread's mask save for ga2_affinity.

Verified: Eigou 1's mv060 (61.8 s, 1852 pictures at 29.97 fps) plays natively in real time with the game at 60 fps
around it, closed through the game's own end path; subtitles drawn (test file); unit tests 661/662.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
